1
00:00:07,268 --> 00:00:09,705
- You all set for tomorrow?
- 12:00 sharp. We're ready.

2
00:00:09,792 --> 00:00:11,054
You talking about lunch?

3
00:00:11,141 --> 00:00:12,838
- That sounds civilized.
- You got the memo.

4
00:00:12,925 --> 00:00:14,492
We're talking about
the mandatory seminar

5
00:00:14,579 --> 00:00:15,798
on budget protocols.

6
00:00:15,885 --> 00:00:17,147
Oh. Have fun with that.

7
00:00:17,234 --> 00:00:18,453
You're coming too, Jane.

8
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:19,802
[Jane]
'You're joking, of course.'

9
00:00:19,889 --> 00:00:21,195
I-I don't do seminars.

10
00:00:21,282 --> 00:00:22,935
Well, you do when
they're mandatory.

11
00:00:23,023 --> 00:00:25,068
- No, I'm a consultant.
- Too bad.

12
00:00:25,155 --> 00:00:27,418
They're checking attendance.
You have to sign in.

13
00:00:27,505 --> 00:00:29,551
Oh, okay then, um..

14
00:00:29,638 --> 00:00:32,902
"Patrick Jane."

15
00:00:32,989 --> 00:00:36,253
Just, uh, copy that down for me.

16
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:38,255
Forge your signature?
That's against the rules.

17
00:00:38,342 --> 00:00:40,605
Is it?
I'm not gonna tell anyone.

18
00:00:40,692 --> 00:00:42,825
- Jane.
- Lisbon.

19
00:00:42,912 --> 00:00:45,001
I understand your
precarious emotional state

20
00:00:45,088 --> 00:00:47,786
given you've just gotten your
job back and your sensitivity

21
00:00:47,873 --> 00:00:50,311
to the bureaucrats that
are watching your every move.

22
00:00:50,398 --> 00:00:52,487
- They are.
- Yes, but that's your thing.

23
00:00:52,574 --> 00:00:54,532
I gotta be me.
I can't change myself.

24
00:00:54,619 --> 00:00:57,492
No, but you can change
where you are tomorrow at 12.

25
00:00:57,579 --> 00:00:58,580
It's not gonna happen.

26
00:00:58,667 --> 00:01:00,582
You think this is funny?

27
00:01:00,669 --> 00:01:02,366
We got a missing child,
Marin County.

28
00:01:02,453 --> 00:01:04,673
Snatched from a school
bus stop two hours ago.

29
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:07,806
The mother asked for us.
Rigsby will meet us downstairs.

30
00:01:07,893 --> 00:01:10,592
Grace, set up a command post.
Liaise with the Marin sheriff.

31
00:01:10,679 --> 00:01:12,159
Tell him we're on our way.

32
00:01:14,857 --> 00:01:18,121
- It's good to have her back.
- Mm. Yes, it is.

33
00:01:18,208 --> 00:01:21,037
[instrumental music]

34
00:01:25,694 --> 00:01:28,697
Our missing boy,
nine years old, only child.

35
00:01:28,784 --> 00:01:31,743
Another kid was walking to
the bus stop, he saw a vehicle

36
00:01:31,830 --> 00:01:34,920
peeling out with our boy
Conner Flint in it.

37
00:01:35,007 --> 00:01:37,227
'The man behind the wheel
was wearing a hoodie.'

38
00:01:37,314 --> 00:01:40,622
- Description on the vehicle?
- Big and dark.

39
00:01:40,709 --> 00:01:43,799
- The kid's eight years old.
- Is it a custody kidnapping?

40
00:01:43,886 --> 00:01:46,976
The woman was widowed two years
ago. Her husband died of cancer.

41
00:01:47,063 --> 00:01:51,328
Looks like there's family money.
There's no ransom demand yet.

42
00:01:51,415 --> 00:01:53,809
- Start with the bus stop?
- Yeah, you and Cho.

43
00:01:53,896 --> 00:01:55,724
Jane and I will
question the family.

44
00:02:02,948 --> 00:02:05,734
- What's the mother's name?
- 'Elizabeth Flint.'

45
00:02:23,795 --> 00:02:26,581
[indistinct chattering]

46
00:02:28,670 --> 00:02:30,976
[gasps]
Patrick! Oh!

47
00:02:31,063 --> 00:02:33,327
- Thank God you're here.
- Hello, Beth.

48
00:02:34,980 --> 00:02:36,068
[Beth sighs]

49
00:02:38,027 --> 00:02:39,898
I have everything
ready for the reading.

50
00:02:39,985 --> 00:02:42,205
I'll do everything
I can to help, I promise

51
00:02:42,292 --> 00:02:46,035
but, uh, I need to you know,
I'm-I'm not a psychic anymore.

52
00:02:46,122 --> 00:02:48,603
What? Wh...what do you mean?

53
00:02:48,690 --> 00:02:53,173
Well, I mean, I'm not...well,
I-I never really was a psychic.

54
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:55,349
No, I'm not...no...
what are you saying?

55
00:02:55,436 --> 00:02:59,657
No, I-I know that-that
you-you are. Look, you..

56
00:02:59,744 --> 00:03:03,052
Please help me find Conner. You
have a connection with him--

57
00:03:03,139 --> 00:03:04,836
- Beth.
- So...can we get started?

58
00:03:04,923 --> 00:03:07,578
- I have this locket and--
- Excuse me, ma'am. I'm sorry.

59
00:03:07,665 --> 00:03:09,319
- I'm so happy you're here.
- Ma'am.

60
00:03:09,406 --> 00:03:11,452
- Would you excuse us?
- I'm glad you're here.

61
00:03:11,539 --> 00:03:12,888
I-I'm sorry.

62
00:03:22,811 --> 00:03:23,942
[exhales deeply]

63
00:03:25,683 --> 00:03:27,381
She's an old client.

64
00:03:27,468 --> 00:03:28,991
Uh, yeah.

65
00:03:29,078 --> 00:03:30,993
We don't have
time for this mess.

66
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:32,821
That boy is out
there somewhere

67
00:03:32,908 --> 00:03:36,520
and this psychic
stuff is a distraction.

68
00:03:36,607 --> 00:03:38,087
I think you'd better leave.

69
00:03:38,174 --> 00:03:39,306
Can't say I disagree.

70
00:03:41,786 --> 00:03:43,527
Hello. Is Beth inside?

71
00:03:43,614 --> 00:03:45,486
And you are..

72
00:03:45,573 --> 00:03:47,879
[Lisbon]
'I'm Agent Lisbon.
We're with the CBI.'

73
00:03:47,966 --> 00:03:50,273
Oh. Nathan Glass.

74
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:52,319
When Beth told me about Conner

75
00:03:52,406 --> 00:03:54,582
I came immediately
to see what I could sense.

76
00:03:54,669 --> 00:03:56,671
- Sense?
- I'm Beth's spiritual advisor.

77
00:03:56,758 --> 00:03:58,542
- A psychic?
- She's expecting me.

78
00:03:58,629 --> 00:03:59,935
Excuse me.

79
00:04:05,070 --> 00:04:06,333
Second thought.

80
00:04:11,686 --> 00:04:14,558
[theme music]

81
00:04:21,478 --> 00:04:23,959
[indistinct chattering]

82
00:04:25,613 --> 00:04:28,485
[dog barking]

83
00:04:31,096 --> 00:04:34,012
[indistinct chattering]

84
00:04:50,681 --> 00:04:54,337
Forensics found the kid's
phone in the bushes over there.

85
00:04:54,424 --> 00:04:57,209
- Has the amber alert gone live?
- 'Yep. No tips yet.'

86
00:04:57,297 --> 00:04:59,777
Deputies shut down the streets
after Conner disappeared.

87
00:04:59,864 --> 00:05:01,562
There's some unpaved
trails in the woods

88
00:05:01,649 --> 00:05:03,128
'that a vehicle
could get through.'

89
00:05:03,215 --> 00:05:04,347
'We got checkpoints up, but..'

90
00:05:08,308 --> 00:05:10,527
[Cho on phone]
We get a ransom demand yet?

91
00:05:10,614 --> 00:05:12,573
No, and I don't
think we're going to.

92
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:14,836
There've been two other
abductions in the bay area

93
00:05:14,923 --> 00:05:16,620
with a similar MO,
young boys snatched

94
00:05:16,707 --> 00:05:18,492
while waiting for the bus.

95
00:05:18,579 --> 00:05:21,103
But there were balloon animals
found at those scenes.

96
00:05:21,190 --> 00:05:23,410
'They think that's how
the guy lured the kids.'

97
00:05:23,497 --> 00:05:25,063
What happened to those boys?

98
00:05:25,150 --> 00:05:27,022
ME estimates both
boys were strangled

99
00:05:27,109 --> 00:05:29,241
approximately 12 hours
after they vanished.

100
00:05:33,028 --> 00:05:34,986
Which means Conner has
only about eight hours.

101
00:05:35,073 --> 00:05:37,946
[indistinct chattering]

102
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:45,867
I talked with Conner
about safety...all the time.

103
00:05:45,954 --> 00:05:48,217
You know,
i-if a stranger grabs you

104
00:05:48,304 --> 00:05:50,828
just kick, punch, scream,
anything to get away.

105
00:05:50,915 --> 00:05:53,265
You know, I-I...I told him.

106
00:05:53,353 --> 00:05:57,313
Shh. It's not your fault.
You taught him well.

107
00:05:57,400 --> 00:06:00,925
Everyone who knows you
knows that you're a perfect mom.

108
00:06:01,012 --> 00:06:02,666
How well did you know Conner?

109
00:06:02,753 --> 00:06:05,016
Beth and I have worked
together for two years

110
00:06:05,103 --> 00:06:07,149
'since her husband passed over.'

111
00:06:07,236 --> 00:06:09,673
I feel like I've
watched him grow up.

112
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:13,242
Conner's such a great kid.
He's kind and funny and smart.

113
00:06:13,329 --> 00:06:16,332
Beth, uh, did Conner always
take the bus to school?

114
00:06:16,419 --> 00:06:18,726
It-it was Deke's idea,
uh, my brother.

115
00:06:18,813 --> 00:06:22,599
Um, he thought
it would do Conner good.

116
00:06:22,686 --> 00:06:24,601
Deke Hutton. He lives here.

117
00:06:24,688 --> 00:06:27,952
Um...yes, ever since James died

118
00:06:28,039 --> 00:06:31,173
'and-and I-I agreed
with him...about the bus.'

119
00:06:32,435 --> 00:06:34,568
You know, I-I didn't want

120
00:06:34,655 --> 00:06:36,657
Conner to grow up sheltered.

121
00:06:36,744 --> 00:06:38,180
And Jonathan supported it too.

122
00:06:38,267 --> 00:06:40,835
Jonathan is my,
um, my grown stepson.

123
00:06:40,922 --> 00:06:42,402
He's, um, Conner's brother.

124
00:06:42,489 --> 00:06:45,274
You know, he...
actually, he owns this house.

125
00:06:45,361 --> 00:06:48,190
He's letting Conner and me
stay as long as we want.

126
00:06:48,277 --> 00:06:50,148
Nice guy.

127
00:06:50,235 --> 00:06:52,107
And where are
Deke and Jonathan now?

128
00:06:52,194 --> 00:06:56,241
Um, they're with
our...our bankers.

129
00:06:56,328 --> 00:07:01,595
If...if this is, uh,
a-a ransom-type thing, I..

130
00:07:01,682 --> 00:07:03,379
we'd need to
have a lotta cash.

131
00:07:03,466 --> 00:07:04,685
Yes, ifit is.

132
00:07:06,948 --> 00:07:09,298
You-you...you can find him.

133
00:07:09,385 --> 00:07:11,343
You-you, you and Nate,
you can work together.

134
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:13,041
'I know that you can--'

135
00:07:13,128 --> 00:07:15,783
I know you can see
where he is, so..

136
00:07:15,870 --> 00:07:18,046
...so-so that we-we
can bring him home.

137
00:07:18,133 --> 00:07:20,396
Mr. Glass, would you excuse us?

138
00:07:20,483 --> 00:07:22,398
Beth, don't worry.
I'll be outside, okay?

139
00:07:22,485 --> 00:07:23,747
Okay.

140
00:07:26,620 --> 00:07:28,491
Beth, please have a seat.

141
00:07:30,406 --> 00:07:31,842
'Okay. Just breathe and relax.'

142
00:07:31,929 --> 00:07:34,715
I need you to hear this...okay?

143
00:07:34,802 --> 00:07:36,978
I'm not a psychic.

144
00:07:37,065 --> 00:07:38,719
I never was.

145
00:07:38,806 --> 00:07:41,243
I was a con artist.

146
00:07:41,330 --> 00:07:43,985
I took your money,
and I told you lies.

147
00:07:44,072 --> 00:07:45,943
- No, they-they weren't lies.
- Yes.

148
00:07:46,030 --> 00:07:48,946
No. No. You-you
know they weren't.

149
00:07:49,033 --> 00:07:50,992
No, i-if you're,
if you're not a psychic

150
00:07:51,079 --> 00:07:54,212
then-then why are you
working with the police?

151
00:07:54,299 --> 00:07:56,519
Ma'am, Mr. Jane
is working with us

152
00:07:56,606 --> 00:07:58,695
because he is
an excellent investigator.

153
00:07:58,782 --> 00:08:00,915
He's gonna be very helpful
in this. I promise.

154
00:08:03,308 --> 00:08:05,833
I understand.

155
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:10,577
I-it must be a terrible burden,
the gift you have.

156
00:08:10,664 --> 00:08:12,970
Of course you have to deny it.

157
00:08:13,057 --> 00:08:16,321
I mean...even St. Peter
denied who he was three times.

158
00:08:16,408 --> 00:08:19,107
Beth, there are no such thing
as psychics. This man Glass--

159
00:08:19,194 --> 00:08:21,152
- It must be awful..
- He's a fraud too.

160
00:08:21,239 --> 00:08:22,937
...knowing what's gonna happen.
I mean, if..

161
00:08:23,024 --> 00:08:25,200
who's gonna live
and who's gonna die.

162
00:08:25,287 --> 00:08:27,855
But please, please..

163
00:08:27,942 --> 00:08:29,900
...pleasedon't deny your gift.

164
00:08:29,987 --> 00:08:32,076
Not now. No.
You have to help me.

165
00:08:32,163 --> 00:08:33,817
You gotta help me find Conner.

166
00:08:33,904 --> 00:08:35,384
Here, look, I have this locket

167
00:08:35,471 --> 00:08:37,604
and it has
his-his first haircut.

168
00:08:37,691 --> 00:08:40,215
Look. Touch this.
See if you can get a sense.

169
00:08:40,302 --> 00:08:41,564
- If this is--
- No, Beth.

170
00:08:41,651 --> 00:08:43,523
This is from his
first haircut and..

171
00:08:43,610 --> 00:08:44,915
- Touch this.
- No.

172
00:08:45,002 --> 00:08:46,526
- Mrs. Flint.
- No! My, no!

173
00:08:46,613 --> 00:08:49,354
My son...no! My son is missing.

174
00:08:49,441 --> 00:08:53,445
[sobbing]
My son is missing! You have
to find him! You have to.

175
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:57,101
Mrs. Flint, please, let's just
sit down for a minute, please..

176
00:08:57,188 --> 00:08:59,277
Calm down, okay? It's okay.

177
00:08:59,364 --> 00:09:02,803
Patrick...I..

178
00:09:02,890 --> 00:09:05,632
[sobbing]

179
00:09:09,853 --> 00:09:12,900
Sources inside the Marin County
sheriff's department confirm

180
00:09:12,987 --> 00:09:15,206
that Conner Flint, age nine

181
00:09:15,293 --> 00:09:18,296
was snatched from his
school bus stop this morning.

182
00:09:18,383 --> 00:09:20,690
No ransom demand
has yet been made.

183
00:09:20,777 --> 00:09:22,953
A CBI spokesman
told this reporter

184
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:25,782
that all leads and tips
are being pursued

185
00:09:25,869 --> 00:09:28,829
and that police are looking
for a possible suspect.

186
00:09:28,916 --> 00:09:31,875
[woman on TV]
'However, when we asked them
to give further information'

187
00:09:31,962 --> 00:09:35,226
'about who that suspect
might be, they refused.'

188
00:09:35,313 --> 00:09:37,359
[man on TV]
'Thanks, Debra. Keep us posted.'

189
00:09:37,446 --> 00:09:39,143
They'd go nuts if we told them

190
00:09:39,230 --> 00:09:41,319
we suspected someone who's
murdered two other boys.

191
00:09:41,406 --> 00:09:43,147
They're calling this
guy the balloon man.

192
00:09:43,234 --> 00:09:45,759
Media. Vultures.

193
00:09:45,846 --> 00:09:47,195
I'm checking into
pedophiles released

194
00:09:47,282 --> 00:09:49,023
before the first killing,
looking for any

195
00:09:49,110 --> 00:09:50,807
escalating violence.
Nothing so far.

196
00:09:50,894 --> 00:09:53,941
Good. Anything from forensics
yet on trace from the bus stop?

197
00:09:54,028 --> 00:09:56,552
Yeah, they say it's gonna
take at least 24 hours.

198
00:09:56,639 --> 00:09:59,642
[sighs]
Okay. A serial offender.
This changes our whole play.

199
00:09:59,729 --> 00:10:01,688
We gotta work
three cases to find him.

200
00:10:01,775 --> 00:10:03,733
I'll check everything
the local cops already checked.

201
00:10:03,820 --> 00:10:05,779
- Maybe they missed something.
- Work fast.

202
00:10:10,348 --> 00:10:13,525
Mr. Flint, when was the last
time you saw your brother?

203
00:10:13,613 --> 00:10:16,267
Uh, this morning
at breakfast.

204
00:10:16,354 --> 00:10:20,750
We have breakfast together,
Beth, Conner, Deke, and me.

205
00:10:20,837 --> 00:10:22,839
Conner had-had French toast.
Everything was fine.

206
00:10:22,926 --> 00:10:25,450
I-I...I can't believe this.

207
00:10:25,537 --> 00:10:29,063
[sighs]
How's-how's Beth doing?

208
00:10:29,150 --> 00:10:30,804
Mm. Not great.

209
00:10:30,891 --> 00:10:33,110
How long ago did
she marry your father?

210
00:10:33,197 --> 00:10:35,025
Um, 12 years ago.

211
00:10:35,112 --> 00:10:37,506
How did you feel about that?

212
00:10:37,593 --> 00:10:41,597
I like and respect Beth, if
that's what you're getting at.

213
00:10:41,684 --> 00:10:44,992
She's no wicked stepmother. I
care deeply for her and Conner.

214
00:10:45,079 --> 00:10:47,037
If you care,
how come you let her

215
00:10:47,124 --> 00:10:49,474
throw her money away
on this, uh, psychic?

216
00:10:49,561 --> 00:10:52,347
Never bothered you
when it was you, Mr. Jane.

217
00:10:52,434 --> 00:10:54,088
Yeah, I heard about you.

218
00:10:54,175 --> 00:10:56,003
You nearly
squeezed Beth dry.

219
00:10:56,090 --> 00:10:57,744
- And you are..
- Conner's uncle.

220
00:10:57,831 --> 00:10:59,397
- Deke Hutton.
- Mm.

221
00:10:59,484 --> 00:11:01,878
And you should've gone to jail,
you miserable sleazebag.

222
00:11:01,965 --> 00:11:05,882
Well, nice to meet you too. I'm
not sure that I'm a sleazebag.

223
00:11:05,969 --> 00:11:07,188
- That's enough.
- 'Miserable--'

224
00:11:07,275 --> 00:11:10,017
We're here to find
Conner, got it?

225
00:11:10,104 --> 00:11:11,714
Yeah. Sorry.

226
00:11:11,801 --> 00:11:13,498
We're trying to put
together Conner's morning.

227
00:11:13,585 --> 00:11:16,850
You dropped him off at
his school bus stop, right?

228
00:11:16,937 --> 00:11:18,155
Yeah.

229
00:11:18,242 --> 00:11:20,941
And you left him there alone?

230
00:11:21,028 --> 00:11:22,594
Yeah.

231
00:11:22,682 --> 00:11:24,684
He wanted it that way.

232
00:11:24,771 --> 00:11:26,250
He wanted to show
his independence.

233
00:11:26,337 --> 00:11:28,557
The other kids
would make fun of him

234
00:11:28,644 --> 00:11:31,081
if he had somebody
waiting with him.

235
00:11:31,168 --> 00:11:33,475
It's such a safe neighborhood.
He's always been fine.

236
00:11:33,562 --> 00:11:35,390
So it was routine for you

237
00:11:35,477 --> 00:11:38,698
to, uh, leave him
alone there?

238
00:11:38,785 --> 00:11:42,527
Yeah. I told you. He wanted
it that way. Beth agreed.

239
00:11:42,614 --> 00:11:46,096
If you think you'll pin this
on me, then you're mistaken!

240
00:11:46,183 --> 00:11:49,534
Typical addict, misdirected
anger, persecution complex.

241
00:11:49,621 --> 00:11:53,190
- Excuse me. I'm not an addict.
- Yes, you are. You both are.

242
00:11:53,277 --> 00:11:55,366
You, gambling, hence
the purple smudge

243
00:11:55,453 --> 00:11:57,934
on your thumb from
the ticket stubs at the track

244
00:11:58,021 --> 00:12:00,241
and your need to live off
your sister's money

245
00:12:00,328 --> 00:12:03,723
and you, antidepressants,
the shiny skin, the dyspepsia.

246
00:12:03,810 --> 00:12:08,292
Some deep emotional need...not
being fulfilled, I would guess.

247
00:12:08,379 --> 00:12:10,120
- Are we done here?
- Just getting started.

248
00:12:10,207 --> 00:12:12,557
Thank you. We are.

249
00:12:12,644 --> 00:12:14,081
[sighs]

250
00:12:15,038 --> 00:12:16,213
[Deke]
Jerk.

251
00:12:20,174 --> 00:12:21,479
Nice work.

252
00:12:21,566 --> 00:12:23,307
[Rigsby]
'I dug up possible witnesses'

253
00:12:23,394 --> 00:12:24,961
'in the first two cases.'

254
00:12:25,048 --> 00:12:26,963
A power company guy
near the first killing

255
00:12:27,050 --> 00:12:28,835
a teacher on the second

256
00:12:28,922 --> 00:12:31,402
and a neighbor
of the second kid, like that.

257
00:12:31,489 --> 00:12:33,840
Long shots. We'd do
better using that psychic.

258
00:12:33,927 --> 00:12:35,363
Thought you liked
that spiritual stuff.

259
00:12:35,450 --> 00:12:36,930
What about your
psychic cousin Yolanda?

260
00:12:37,017 --> 00:12:38,714
Yolanda's real.
That guy's a fake.

261
00:12:38,801 --> 00:12:41,673
- Good luck.
- You too.

262
00:12:41,761 --> 00:12:44,241
Mr. Walton, we understand
the day the first boy vanished

263
00:12:44,328 --> 00:12:46,722
you were checking a downed
power line on Martindale Road.

264
00:12:46,809 --> 00:12:48,289
Yep. That's what my records say.

265
00:12:48,376 --> 00:12:49,943
You know,
funny story about that.

266
00:12:50,030 --> 00:12:52,597
They told me it was
a damaged overhead conductor.

267
00:12:52,684 --> 00:12:55,426
Turns out it was
a blown transformer.

268
00:12:55,513 --> 00:12:58,429
[chuckles]
Can you imagine? I could have
taken out the entire grid.

269
00:12:58,516 --> 00:12:59,735
Think back.

270
00:12:59,822 --> 00:13:01,302
Did you happen
to notice anything

271
00:13:01,389 --> 00:13:03,478
on your way to or from that job

272
00:13:03,565 --> 00:13:05,610
or maybe this child?

273
00:13:05,697 --> 00:13:07,569
I'm not sure.
What's the kid's name?

274
00:13:10,398 --> 00:13:11,965
Reggie Miranda.

275
00:13:12,052 --> 00:13:13,270
He was the second victim.

276
00:13:13,357 --> 00:13:15,577
Your car got a flat tire
on Teer's Hill.

277
00:13:15,664 --> 00:13:17,361
Remember seeing
him at the bus stop?

278
00:13:17,448 --> 00:13:21,235
Well, that wasn't
a flat tire per se.

279
00:13:21,322 --> 00:13:24,151
More like, uh,
I told my girlfriend that

280
00:13:24,238 --> 00:13:25,892
so we'd be stranded

281
00:13:25,979 --> 00:13:27,458
she could get
a little friendlier

282
00:13:27,545 --> 00:13:30,548
which she did,
if you know what I mean.

283
00:13:30,635 --> 00:13:31,767
High five.

284
00:13:31,854 --> 00:13:34,683
Come on. Give it up.

285
00:13:34,770 --> 00:13:37,120
As I was leaving,
there was this black SUV

286
00:13:37,207 --> 00:13:38,861
nearly ran me off the road

287
00:13:38,948 --> 00:13:40,689
which reminds me
of another funny story..

288
00:13:43,910 --> 00:13:45,389
Black SUV,
power company guy says

289
00:13:45,476 --> 00:13:47,174
there was a ding
in the bumper.

290
00:13:47,261 --> 00:13:48,958
Great. That narrows it down.

291
00:13:56,792 --> 00:13:58,968
I think I can help you.

292
00:13:59,055 --> 00:14:00,796
Take my hand.

293
00:14:00,883 --> 00:14:02,580
I want a baby
more than anything.

294
00:14:02,667 --> 00:14:06,280
Shh. I know.
Just...listen.

295
00:14:09,544 --> 00:14:11,763
[sighs]

296
00:14:11,851 --> 00:14:13,156
[exhales deeply]

297
00:14:15,463 --> 00:14:17,726
In the beyond, Beth,
I see your baby.

298
00:14:20,642 --> 00:14:22,600
'He's the light of your life.'

299
00:14:22,687 --> 00:14:24,341
He? It's a boy.

300
00:14:24,428 --> 00:14:26,430
Yes, a boy.

301
00:14:28,737 --> 00:14:30,695
[exhales deeply]

302
00:14:30,782 --> 00:14:33,220
His name is Conner.

303
00:14:33,307 --> 00:14:34,961
Conner? That-that's
my father's name.

304
00:14:35,048 --> 00:14:36,092
[chuckles]

305
00:14:45,928 --> 00:14:47,974
A beautiful baby boy.

306
00:14:48,061 --> 00:14:50,890
[chuckling]

307
00:15:09,821 --> 00:15:12,302
'That was Conner's favorite
when he was a baby.'

308
00:15:12,389 --> 00:15:14,609
He doesn't play with
it anymore, but I just

309
00:15:14,696 --> 00:15:17,177
I can't throw it out now.
You understand.

310
00:15:17,264 --> 00:15:20,049
Yeah. Here.

311
00:15:20,136 --> 00:15:22,051
[sighs]

312
00:15:22,138 --> 00:15:24,662
You know, Deke thinks
I'm an idiot about you.

313
00:15:24,749 --> 00:15:27,839
Jonathan probably does too,
but he's too nice to say so.

314
00:15:27,927 --> 00:15:29,406
You know,
but they weren't there.

315
00:15:29,493 --> 00:15:33,019
They didn't, they didn't
see your powers at work.

316
00:15:33,106 --> 00:15:34,498
There was nothing to see.

317
00:15:36,631 --> 00:15:40,504
Women that are trying hard
to have babies often succeed

318
00:15:40,591 --> 00:15:45,553
and when they do, there's
a 50/50 chance that it's a boy.

319
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:48,817
- It was just a good guess.
- No, you knew.

320
00:15:48,904 --> 00:15:52,734
And what was I to say, you
were never gonna have a child?

321
00:15:52,821 --> 00:15:54,997
Nobody wants
a gloomy psychic.

322
00:16:00,350 --> 00:16:02,787
You had a child.
You lost her.

323
00:16:02,874 --> 00:16:05,399
I-I read about it
in the papers.

324
00:16:05,486 --> 00:16:09,011
- Murdered?
- Yeah.

325
00:16:09,098 --> 00:16:10,186
[whispers]
I'm sorry.

326
00:16:10,273 --> 00:16:11,840
[whispers]
Yeah.

327
00:16:11,927 --> 00:16:14,756
- That's why you deny your gift?
- No.

328
00:16:14,843 --> 00:16:16,627
Is Conner dead too?
Please. I'm sorry.

329
00:16:16,714 --> 00:16:18,673
I'm sorry about before,
but please tell me.

330
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:20,980
- It's just us right now--
- I-I can't tell you.

331
00:16:21,067 --> 00:16:23,286
[panting]
Beth. Oh, thank God.

332
00:16:23,373 --> 00:16:24,940
I had a flash, and, uh..

333
00:16:25,027 --> 00:16:27,377
[Lisbon]
Mr. Glass, I told
you to stay downstairs.

334
00:16:27,464 --> 00:16:29,379
Beth, I think I saw Conner.

335
00:16:29,466 --> 00:16:31,207
It was just a flash,
but, um..

336
00:16:31,294 --> 00:16:33,470
Oh, please, Beth,
don't listen to this nonsense.

337
00:16:33,557 --> 00:16:35,907
[Beth]
'Where's he? Where-where
is he? Is-is he alive?'

338
00:16:35,995 --> 00:16:38,475
I don't know.
It was just a split second.

339
00:16:38,562 --> 00:16:42,218
I need a vessel
or...Conner's favorite.

340
00:16:43,567 --> 00:16:45,569
From when he was a baby,
of course.

341
00:16:45,656 --> 00:16:48,224
Of course. Nice read.

342
00:16:48,311 --> 00:16:50,009
- Mr. Glass, let's go.
- No, Agent Lisbon.

343
00:16:50,096 --> 00:16:51,880
Please, no, Nate,
tell me. Go ahead.

344
00:16:51,967 --> 00:16:54,404
Beth, it's alright. I'm here.

345
00:16:54,491 --> 00:16:56,711
[sighs]
I need you to
think with me, okay?

346
00:16:56,798 --> 00:16:58,887
I need you to think of Conner.

347
00:16:58,974 --> 00:17:01,020
He's filling your heart.

348
00:17:01,107 --> 00:17:04,588
He's filling your mind..

349
00:17:04,675 --> 00:17:05,850
[inhales]

350
00:17:07,113 --> 00:17:08,288
Yes.

351
00:17:09,724 --> 00:17:11,073
Yes, I see him.

352
00:17:12,901 --> 00:17:15,077
[Glass]
'He's very still.'

353
00:17:15,164 --> 00:17:17,079
He's dead?

354
00:17:17,166 --> 00:17:19,429
No.

355
00:17:19,516 --> 00:17:21,344
He's alive.

356
00:17:21,431 --> 00:17:23,825
Sleeping.

357
00:17:23,912 --> 00:17:25,696
[shouting]
Conner, wake up!

358
00:17:25,783 --> 00:17:27,872
Can you hear me?
Your mother's here!

359
00:17:31,876 --> 00:17:35,010
He's saying,
"I love you, mo mo."

360
00:17:35,097 --> 00:17:38,231
Mo mo. That's what he called me.
He calls me mo mo.

361
00:17:38,318 --> 00:17:41,147
Oh! Oh!

362
00:17:41,234 --> 00:17:43,714
- 'Thank you.'
- Yeah.

363
00:17:43,801 --> 00:17:45,325
[sighs]

364
00:17:45,412 --> 00:17:47,240
- Hallelujah.
- Mmm.

365
00:17:47,327 --> 00:17:48,632
Amen.

366
00:17:54,377 --> 00:17:56,379
Jonathan! Jonathan!

367
00:17:56,466 --> 00:17:59,121
Jonathan, he's alive.
Conner's alive. Nate sensed him.

368
00:17:59,208 --> 00:18:02,342
Oh, Nate sensed
something alright...money.

369
00:18:02,429 --> 00:18:04,387
- You think Glass was faking?
- 'Course he was.

370
00:18:04,474 --> 00:18:06,650
- Money-grubbin' bastard.
- No, no, no.

371
00:18:06,737 --> 00:18:08,696
It was Conner.
He-he called me mo mo.

372
00:18:08,783 --> 00:18:11,960
That-that's his nickname
for me. N-nobody knew that.

373
00:18:12,047 --> 00:18:15,137
That's exactly how
the trick works, Beth.

374
00:18:15,224 --> 00:18:18,358
You use a detail that
no one could possibly know

375
00:18:18,445 --> 00:18:21,274
except Nate Glass did know.

376
00:18:21,361 --> 00:18:24,059
He's been in and out
of this house for two years.

377
00:18:24,146 --> 00:18:26,496
No, I don't think
he knew that name. No..

378
00:18:26,583 --> 00:18:29,020
How much have you paid him
since your husband died?

379
00:18:29,108 --> 00:18:32,328
How much more will you give him
since he can sense your son?

380
00:18:32,415 --> 00:18:34,156
And then, if Conner dies

381
00:18:34,243 --> 00:18:36,376
and Glass can contact his spirit

382
00:18:36,463 --> 00:18:37,725
what won't you give?

383
00:18:37,812 --> 00:18:39,857
Hey, don't say that.
Don't you dare.

384
00:18:39,944 --> 00:18:42,556
You're sick.
Nate would never do that.

385
00:18:42,643 --> 00:18:44,558
Of course, he would. Believe me.

386
00:18:44,645 --> 00:18:45,602
[chuckles]
He would.

387
00:18:45,689 --> 00:18:47,038
No, you don't know, Patrick.

388
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:48,649
Apparently, you
don't know anything.

389
00:18:48,736 --> 00:18:50,259
My son called out for me.

390
00:18:50,346 --> 00:18:52,087
He's alive,
but you won't believe it

391
00:18:52,174 --> 00:18:54,002
because you can't
stand what you are

392
00:18:54,089 --> 00:18:55,656
so you run away
from yourself

393
00:18:55,743 --> 00:18:58,485
and you hate anybody like you,
and hurt anybody who cares.

394
00:18:58,572 --> 00:19:00,051
That doesn't mean
I'm psychic.

395
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:01,923
It just means you're
gullible and desperate.

396
00:19:02,010 --> 00:19:04,839
What is wrong with you
that you treat people like that?

397
00:19:04,926 --> 00:19:07,320
Oh, you should've
seen me ten years ago.

398
00:19:12,803 --> 00:19:13,978
[birds chirping]

399
00:19:18,157 --> 00:19:20,724
It's beautiful, huh?

400
00:19:20,811 --> 00:19:22,900
It's all state
forests that way.

401
00:19:22,987 --> 00:19:26,687
Nothing but bears
and deer...elk.

402
00:19:26,774 --> 00:19:29,298
Hmm.

403
00:19:29,385 --> 00:19:32,910
You're pretty good.
I'll give you that.

404
00:19:32,997 --> 00:19:36,175
Not great.
Just...pretty good.

405
00:19:36,262 --> 00:19:38,133
What can I say?
It's a gift.

406
00:19:38,220 --> 00:19:39,961
Yeah.

407
00:19:40,048 --> 00:19:41,136
Here's the thing, Glass.

408
00:19:41,223 --> 00:19:42,920
I played the same game myself

409
00:19:43,007 --> 00:19:46,010
so normally, I wouldn't tell you
not to run your little scam.

410
00:19:46,097 --> 00:19:47,838
- It's not a scam.
- 'It's a scam.'

411
00:19:47,925 --> 00:19:50,928
We both know it's a scam,
but you stepped over a line.

412
00:19:51,015 --> 00:19:53,714
This is police business. There's
a child's life at stake here.

413
00:19:53,801 --> 00:19:55,672
Yeah, that's why I'm here.

414
00:19:55,759 --> 00:19:58,719
You don't want to push me.

415
00:19:58,806 --> 00:20:00,938
Back off this woman.

416
00:20:01,025 --> 00:20:05,769
Get out of here right now
or you're gonna regret it.

417
00:20:05,856 --> 00:20:08,903
I can understand
your frustration.

418
00:20:08,990 --> 00:20:11,688
You had the vision
and you lost it, and I..

419
00:20:11,775 --> 00:20:13,864
...I can't think
of anything more horrible.

420
00:20:13,951 --> 00:20:16,650
You got a lot of nerve.

421
00:20:16,737 --> 00:20:19,087
Maybe I've got you
pegged all wrong.

422
00:20:19,174 --> 00:20:21,481
Maybe you're
a kidnapper too.

423
00:20:21,568 --> 00:20:24,745
Yeah. No, he's not the balloon
man. I talked to Van Pelt.

424
00:20:24,832 --> 00:20:27,791
During the first two abductions,
he was in New York and Atlanta

425
00:20:27,878 --> 00:20:29,880
giving a presentation
before a 100 people.

426
00:20:29,967 --> 00:20:31,621
Actually, it was 200.

427
00:20:31,708 --> 00:20:33,232
Yeah.

428
00:20:33,319 --> 00:20:34,450
Excuse me.

429
00:20:37,279 --> 00:20:40,543
We don't have time for you
to have a feud with this guy.

430
00:20:40,630 --> 00:20:42,980
I-it's like your conscience
is battling your old self.

431
00:20:43,067 --> 00:20:45,548
There's no upside.

432
00:20:45,635 --> 00:20:47,115
You think
that's why I'm here?

433
00:20:47,202 --> 00:20:48,943
- That's intriguing.
- 'We have to go.'

434
00:20:49,030 --> 00:20:51,467
A boy's life's on
the line and this man could

435
00:20:51,554 --> 00:20:52,990
take another kid and kill him.

436
00:20:53,077 --> 00:20:54,644
Yeah. Let's go then.

437
00:20:56,385 --> 00:20:58,387
So I've been trolling
pedophile chat rooms.

438
00:20:58,474 --> 00:21:01,390
There's this one guy, Charlie95.
Something's up with him.

439
00:21:01,477 --> 00:21:03,914
He's too eager to chat
about the first two boys.

440
00:21:04,001 --> 00:21:05,176
- Are you tracking him?
- Yep.

441
00:21:05,264 --> 00:21:07,178
IT says any minute now.

442
00:21:07,266 --> 00:21:08,702
Tell me you've
got something better.

443
00:21:08,789 --> 00:21:10,312
Been looking
into this black SUV

444
00:21:10,399 --> 00:21:12,488
the power company guy saw,
cross-checking to see

445
00:21:12,575 --> 00:21:15,665
if any registered
pedophiles own one.

446
00:21:15,752 --> 00:21:17,014
- 'It's thin.'
- Yeah, it's thin.

447
00:21:17,101 --> 00:21:18,799
We're not gonna make it, are we?

448
00:21:18,886 --> 00:21:21,497
Jane, feel free
to jump in any time.

449
00:21:21,584 --> 00:21:23,586
I'm thinking.

450
00:21:23,673 --> 00:21:25,240
[inhales deeply]

451
00:21:25,327 --> 00:21:27,764
The second boy, Reggie,
it's bothering me.

452
00:21:27,851 --> 00:21:30,811
If he reached the bus stop
just three minutes later

453
00:21:30,898 --> 00:21:33,509
he would've arrived at
the same time as his classmate

454
00:21:33,596 --> 00:21:35,729
and Reggie would
still be alive today.

455
00:21:35,816 --> 00:21:37,600
- 'Is that bad luck?'
- Or planning.

456
00:21:37,687 --> 00:21:39,863
Maybe the killer was watching
for the perfect moment.

457
00:21:39,950 --> 00:21:41,909
How could anyone have
watched the first kid?

458
00:21:41,996 --> 00:21:44,215
His bus stop's not
visible from the main road.

459
00:21:44,303 --> 00:21:47,131
I've got a picture of the first
crime scene somewhere here.

460
00:21:47,218 --> 00:21:49,569
Charlie95 is Brady Walton

461
00:21:49,656 --> 00:21:51,179
'the power company guy
we questioned.'

462
00:21:51,266 --> 00:21:54,008
- 'It can't be a coincidence.'
- 'It isn't.'

463
00:21:54,095 --> 00:21:56,793
'The killer was watching
from above.'

464
00:21:58,839 --> 00:22:00,406
Walton is the Balloon Man.

465
00:22:00,493 --> 00:22:02,799
Oh, my God.
He was here. We had him.

466
00:22:02,886 --> 00:22:05,846
Get Cho on the phone. Tell him
we're moving in immediately.

467
00:22:15,682 --> 00:22:17,379
Walton's registered four guns
including an AK.

468
00:22:17,466 --> 00:22:19,207
No telling how many
he's really got.

469
00:22:19,294 --> 00:22:21,252
Good to know.
Here's how it's gonna work.

470
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:23,777
Van Pelt and I are gonna take
the three-four corner.

471
00:22:23,864 --> 00:22:25,822
You and Cho are gonna take
the one-two.

472
00:22:25,909 --> 00:22:28,347
Now be careful.
The kid could still be in there.

473
00:22:43,362 --> 00:22:45,146
[machine gun firing]

474
00:22:53,981 --> 00:22:55,330
You ain't gettin' me!

475
00:22:55,417 --> 00:22:57,463
Not gonna happen!

476
00:22:57,550 --> 00:22:59,508
[Van Pelt]
'Cho, do you copy?'

477
00:23:06,341 --> 00:23:08,387
[panting]
Lisbon, we're pinned.

478
00:23:08,474 --> 00:23:10,476
We're pinned
on the two side.

479
00:23:10,563 --> 00:23:13,435
Take the three corner. Let me
know when you're in position.

480
00:23:13,522 --> 00:23:14,871
[firing continues]

481
00:23:17,657 --> 00:23:19,920
[firing continues]

482
00:23:20,007 --> 00:23:21,791
[panting]

483
00:23:23,489 --> 00:23:25,882
Rigs, I got a clear path
to the front door.

484
00:23:25,969 --> 00:23:26,927
Stand by.

485
00:23:27,014 --> 00:23:28,407
[cocks gun]

486
00:23:28,494 --> 00:23:29,408
[casings clatter]

487
00:23:31,845 --> 00:23:35,283
[Walton]
'It may be too late for me,
but I ain't going to prison!'

488
00:23:35,370 --> 00:23:37,285
'I ain't going quiet!'

489
00:23:40,070 --> 00:23:42,682
Approaching the door.
Stand by.

490
00:23:42,769 --> 00:23:46,033
[panting]
Van Pelt,
are you in position?

491
00:23:46,120 --> 00:23:47,077
Van Pelt?

492
00:23:49,558 --> 00:23:50,864
Van Pelt?

493
00:23:54,258 --> 00:23:55,564
Van Pelt?

494
00:23:57,914 --> 00:23:59,089
Screw you..

495
00:23:59,176 --> 00:24:01,048
[gunshot]
Oh!

496
00:24:08,751 --> 00:24:10,100
[coughs]

497
00:24:11,841 --> 00:24:13,277
Everybody okay?

498
00:24:13,364 --> 00:24:14,975
Find the kid.

499
00:24:16,672 --> 00:24:17,891
Conner?

500
00:24:17,978 --> 00:24:19,283
- Lisbon!
- 'Conner?'

501
00:24:19,370 --> 00:24:21,677
[panting]
I'm alright. Walton's down.

502
00:24:21,764 --> 00:24:23,505
[coughs]

503
00:24:23,592 --> 00:24:25,376
Walton, stay with us.

504
00:24:25,464 --> 00:24:26,421
[coughs]

505
00:24:26,508 --> 00:24:29,511
Where's the kid? Tell us.

506
00:24:29,598 --> 00:24:31,513
Where's Conner?

507
00:24:31,600 --> 00:24:32,993
[strained]
How would I know?

508
00:24:33,080 --> 00:24:35,691
He's lying. Gotta be.

509
00:24:35,778 --> 00:24:38,477
Boss, the house is clear.
The kid's not in there.

510
00:24:38,564 --> 00:24:40,783
[cell phone rings]

511
00:24:43,873 --> 00:24:45,962
Hey, Jane.

512
00:24:46,049 --> 00:24:48,835
We got Walton.
The kid's nowhere to be seen.

513
00:24:48,922 --> 00:24:52,142
Tell Rigsby to look in his left
pocket. There should be a note.

514
00:24:55,494 --> 00:24:58,192
Rigs, is there a note
in your left pants pocket?

515
00:25:03,197 --> 00:25:05,939
"The Balloon Man
didn't take Conner."

516
00:25:06,026 --> 00:25:07,897
Okay, so how'd he do that?

517
00:25:14,164 --> 00:25:17,428
Hey. So videotape puts Brady
Walton at a 7-Eleven across town

518
00:25:17,516 --> 00:25:18,952
while Conner
was being snatched.

519
00:25:19,039 --> 00:25:20,867
- Damn it.
- Yeah.

520
00:25:20,954 --> 00:25:23,130
Walton killed those two boys,
but didn't take Conner.

521
00:25:23,217 --> 00:25:25,219
- We've got a copycat.
- So Jane was right.

522
00:25:25,306 --> 00:25:27,351
[sighs]
Jane was right.

523
00:25:27,438 --> 00:25:29,658
I gotta find Lisbon.
She's not in her office.

524
00:25:29,745 --> 00:25:31,834
Hey, Grace,
well done anyway.

525
00:25:31,921 --> 00:25:34,402
You took down
a seriously bad guy.

526
00:25:34,489 --> 00:25:36,273
Another day,
another dollar.

527
00:25:36,360 --> 00:25:37,753
Hey.

528
00:25:37,840 --> 00:25:39,276
You okay?

529
00:25:39,363 --> 00:25:42,279
Yeah. I feel
pretty good actually.

530
00:25:42,366 --> 00:25:45,065
I'm starting to enjoy
shooting people.

531
00:25:47,328 --> 00:25:49,678
[chuckles]
Gotcha.

532
00:25:49,765 --> 00:25:52,028
- No, you didn't.
- Yes, I did.

533
00:25:52,115 --> 00:25:53,508
You didn't get me.

534
00:25:53,595 --> 00:25:54,944
Yeah, I did.

535
00:26:01,385 --> 00:26:03,605
Walton has an alibi
for Conner's abduction.

536
00:26:03,692 --> 00:26:05,215
- 'Hmm.'
- How did you know?

537
00:26:05,302 --> 00:26:08,088
Well, something was just,
uh, a little off.

538
00:26:08,175 --> 00:26:10,873
The other kids Walton killed
were older. They had dark hair.

539
00:26:10,960 --> 00:26:13,833
- That's it?
- Just a good guess.

540
00:26:13,920 --> 00:26:15,661
Why the hell
didn't you tell me?

541
00:26:15,748 --> 00:26:17,184
Would you have done
anything differently?

542
00:26:17,271 --> 00:26:19,229
Probably not. Walton was bad.

543
00:26:19,316 --> 00:26:20,927
[slurps]

544
00:26:21,014 --> 00:26:23,016
Then there's no need
to be cranky.

545
00:26:23,103 --> 00:26:25,409
So who took Conner?

546
00:26:25,496 --> 00:26:27,194
Don't know.
I'm still working on that.

547
00:26:27,281 --> 00:26:30,110
- Is he alive?
- I hope so.

548
00:26:30,197 --> 00:26:32,547
So we're back to square one
on this one.

549
00:26:32,634 --> 00:26:34,288
First principle, motive.

550
00:26:34,375 --> 00:26:37,030
Why would somebody vanish
a nine-year-old boy?

551
00:26:37,117 --> 00:26:39,119
To hide evidence
he was beaten, maybe?

552
00:26:39,206 --> 00:26:41,164
Abuse? Meh. No.

553
00:26:41,251 --> 00:26:46,039
This has the whiff of something
more tangled, more interesting.

554
00:26:46,126 --> 00:26:48,868
Money? We dismissed it because
there was no ransom demand

555
00:26:48,955 --> 00:26:50,957
but there's other ways
to get money.

556
00:26:51,044 --> 00:26:53,437
Conner inherited half
your husband's estate.

557
00:26:53,524 --> 00:26:56,353
Isn't that right, Mrs. Flint?
Twenty million dollars?

558
00:26:56,440 --> 00:26:59,966
Uh, uh, yes. It's being held
in a trust until he turns 30.

559
00:27:00,053 --> 00:27:03,273
- Why?
- Who inherits if Conner dies?

560
00:27:03,360 --> 00:27:05,058
He's.. No, he's just
a little boy.

561
00:27:05,145 --> 00:27:07,887
He's not supposed to
die at all. Wh..

562
00:27:07,974 --> 00:27:09,889
According to the terms
of the trust

563
00:27:09,976 --> 00:27:11,630
you get everything.

564
00:27:11,717 --> 00:27:14,023
Are you saying I..
that I killed my son?

565
00:27:14,110 --> 00:27:16,025
The thing is, we looked
into everybody

566
00:27:16,112 --> 00:27:18,549
in the family's financials.

567
00:27:18,637 --> 00:27:21,509
Jonathan's worth $30 million

568
00:27:21,596 --> 00:27:23,554
but you need money,
don't you, Mrs. Flint?

569
00:27:23,642 --> 00:27:25,600
I-I don't..
I don't know what you mean.

570
00:27:25,687 --> 00:27:28,037
I-I don't know what
I'm doing in this room.

571
00:27:28,124 --> 00:27:30,736
According to the bank
you have $100,000

572
00:27:30,823 --> 00:27:33,260
in credit card debt.

573
00:27:33,347 --> 00:27:37,481
You've spent everything your
husband left you, and then some.

574
00:27:37,568 --> 00:27:40,180
I've made some..
some bad investments

575
00:27:40,267 --> 00:27:42,225
and I-I'm just
not very good with numbers.

576
00:27:42,312 --> 00:27:44,663
I always relied
on James for that.

577
00:27:44,750 --> 00:27:46,360
Could you please sit down?

578
00:27:52,061 --> 00:27:53,410
Thank you.

579
00:27:55,369 --> 00:27:57,327
That must have been
really stressful for you

580
00:27:57,414 --> 00:27:58,633
your financial situation.

581
00:27:58,720 --> 00:28:01,114
It's very embarrassing.

582
00:28:01,201 --> 00:28:03,290
I mean, I couldn't
even tell Deke.

583
00:28:03,377 --> 00:28:06,032
[knock on door]

584
00:28:06,119 --> 00:28:08,121
Uh, could you excuse me?

585
00:28:11,864 --> 00:28:13,517
Her family's here
with a lawyer.

586
00:28:13,604 --> 00:28:16,303
We gotta charge her
or kick her.

587
00:28:21,221 --> 00:28:23,136
Maybe you snapped.

588
00:28:23,223 --> 00:28:25,225
It's understandable.

589
00:28:25,312 --> 00:28:27,793
One weak moment,
and you saw a way out.

590
00:28:27,880 --> 00:28:29,577
If something were
to happen to Conner

591
00:28:29,664 --> 00:28:32,406
all your problems
would be over.

592
00:28:32,493 --> 00:28:36,671
If something happens to Conner,
my lifewill beover.

593
00:28:36,758 --> 00:28:39,718
Please, please..
Just help me find my boy.

594
00:28:42,982 --> 00:28:43,896
[sighs]

595
00:28:47,160 --> 00:28:49,336
- Are you okay?
- I'm fine. I'm fine. Hi.

596
00:28:49,423 --> 00:28:50,424
[kisses]

597
00:28:50,511 --> 00:28:52,165
What did they want?

598
00:28:52,252 --> 00:28:56,082
Well, they a-asked me a lot
of questions about money.

599
00:28:56,169 --> 00:28:57,997
[Lisbon]
'Mom's clean.
What are you thinking?'

600
00:28:58,084 --> 00:29:00,434
[Jane]
'What was I thinking?'

601
00:29:00,521 --> 00:29:03,132
I was thinking, uh...

602
00:29:03,219 --> 00:29:05,352
Love is strange..

603
00:29:05,439 --> 00:29:08,050
...and I was thinking
about a sandwich.

604
00:29:09,791 --> 00:29:13,012
You know who else is profiting
from Conner's abduction?

605
00:29:13,099 --> 00:29:14,665
- Who?
- Nathan Glass.

606
00:29:14,753 --> 00:29:17,103
He alibied out
for the first two kids

607
00:29:17,190 --> 00:29:19,192
but not Conner,
and maybe he took him

608
00:29:19,279 --> 00:29:21,281
to cement his relationship
with Beth.

609
00:29:21,368 --> 00:29:23,109
Well, he's certainly
heartless enough.

610
00:29:23,196 --> 00:29:26,025
- We'll get him in a room.
- No, he'll just clam up.

611
00:29:26,112 --> 00:29:28,505
What if we get him
to lead us to Conner?

612
00:29:28,592 --> 00:29:30,116
That would be nice.

613
00:29:30,203 --> 00:29:31,944
Boss, forensics came back
with the labs

614
00:29:32,031 --> 00:29:33,859
on Conner's school bus stop.

615
00:29:33,946 --> 00:29:34,903
Nothing?

616
00:29:34,990 --> 00:29:36,600
Nope. The only weird thing is

617
00:29:36,687 --> 00:29:38,515
there were traces
of white fir pollen

618
00:29:38,602 --> 00:29:40,039
'where they think
Conner was grabbed.'

619
00:29:40,126 --> 00:29:41,780
No white firs there.
Just pines.

620
00:29:41,867 --> 00:29:44,260
- Alright. Thanks.
- Okay.

621
00:29:46,436 --> 00:29:49,048
Yes. Got it.

622
00:29:50,658 --> 00:29:51,615
[clatters]

623
00:29:54,488 --> 00:29:56,707
Thank you, Caroline.

624
00:29:56,795 --> 00:29:59,188
[sighs]
Let's get out of here.

625
00:29:59,275 --> 00:30:00,886
Any news?

626
00:30:00,973 --> 00:30:02,975
No, uh, listen,
I just wanted to say

627
00:30:03,062 --> 00:30:05,325
I'm sorry for everything
that's happened.

628
00:30:05,412 --> 00:30:08,328
- What's the matter?
- Nothing.

629
00:30:08,415 --> 00:30:12,245
- Uh, bye.
- Wait. Wait. No, Patrick.

630
00:30:12,332 --> 00:30:14,508
- When you grabbed my hand--
- Nothing happened at all.

631
00:30:14,595 --> 00:30:15,814
- Something happened. Are you--
- No!

632
00:30:15,901 --> 00:30:17,728
No, no. Are you
sensing something?

633
00:30:17,816 --> 00:30:19,774
- No. No.
- Liar. Liar.

634
00:30:23,082 --> 00:30:25,736
I see..

635
00:30:25,824 --> 00:30:27,608
There's a face.

636
00:30:29,828 --> 00:30:31,220
What's wrong?

637
00:30:31,307 --> 00:30:32,308
It's Conner.

638
00:30:32,395 --> 00:30:34,006
- It is?
- Oh, my God.

639
00:30:34,093 --> 00:30:35,311
Jane, what are you doing?

640
00:30:35,398 --> 00:30:37,139
I don't understand.

641
00:30:37,226 --> 00:30:39,141
He's standing right there
in front of me.

642
00:30:39,228 --> 00:30:43,450
[panting]
Lisbon.

643
00:30:43,537 --> 00:30:45,974
- What is it?
- Lisbon, I don't like this.

644
00:30:46,061 --> 00:30:48,455
- I don't like this.
- What's going on?

645
00:30:48,542 --> 00:30:51,110
'No. There's someone there.
I see someone.'

646
00:30:51,197 --> 00:30:54,461
Oh, wait. Wait.
There's someone.

647
00:30:54,548 --> 00:30:56,724
Are.. they're following.

648
00:30:56,811 --> 00:30:58,508
They're gonna catch me.

649
00:30:58,595 --> 00:31:00,075
Sweating.

650
00:31:00,162 --> 00:31:02,338
- His abductor?
- Oh, come on. This is crap.

651
00:31:02,425 --> 00:31:03,426
Shh.

652
00:31:03,513 --> 00:31:04,863
[breathing heavily]

653
00:31:07,953 --> 00:31:09,345
I can't do it.

654
00:31:09,432 --> 00:31:11,608
I can't do it.
He's just a little boy.

655
00:31:11,695 --> 00:31:13,610
I-I..

656
00:31:13,697 --> 00:31:16,613
Conner. Conner.

657
00:31:16,700 --> 00:31:18,920
Yes, yes. Conner. Conner.
Where is Conner?

658
00:31:19,007 --> 00:31:22,750
There's a.. There's a light,
and it dances.

659
00:31:22,837 --> 00:31:25,231
It just dance..
It dances on the water.

660
00:31:25,318 --> 00:31:27,059
- It's dancing on the water.
- Oh, god.

661
00:31:27,146 --> 00:31:29,148
- It's so beautiful.
- Conner. Conner's near water.

662
00:31:29,235 --> 00:31:32,455
It's a strong smell, like..

663
00:31:32,542 --> 00:31:34,544
...spicy, like Christmas--

664
00:31:34,631 --> 00:31:35,763
Pine trees?

665
00:31:35,850 --> 00:31:38,505
It's like pine trees,
but different.

666
00:31:38,592 --> 00:31:43,075
Oh, and the bad.. There's
a bad smell, a bad taste.

667
00:31:43,162 --> 00:31:44,772
Pungent.

668
00:31:44,859 --> 00:31:47,079
Gunpowder.
Yeah, it's gunpowder.

669
00:31:47,166 --> 00:31:49,081
It's bad.

670
00:31:49,168 --> 00:31:50,691
[gasps]

671
00:31:50,778 --> 00:31:52,301
[exhales deeply]

672
00:31:52,388 --> 00:31:55,348
And you can almost see
the house.

673
00:31:55,435 --> 00:31:58,133
He's just surrounded.
There's wood, wood and trees.

674
00:31:58,220 --> 00:32:00,614
And-and..

675
00:32:00,701 --> 00:32:03,486
[sighs]

676
00:32:03,573 --> 00:32:07,490
Uh, he's in a cabin.
It's not a cabin.

677
00:32:07,577 --> 00:32:10,841
No, it's like a, uh,
it's smaller, like a sh..

678
00:32:10,929 --> 00:32:12,452
Oh! I'm tired.

679
00:32:12,539 --> 00:32:15,455
Jane. Wake up.

680
00:32:15,542 --> 00:32:18,240
'Jane, wake up!'

681
00:32:18,327 --> 00:32:20,025
- 'What happened?'
- 'I don't know.'

682
00:32:20,112 --> 00:32:22,418
I was gonna ask you that.
That was weird.

683
00:32:22,505 --> 00:32:25,421
- I knew you could sense him.
- Please don't touch me.

684
00:32:25,508 --> 00:32:27,989
Get all of your neighbors
and volunteers.

685
00:32:28,076 --> 00:32:30,296
'Karl, I want you to call
the sheriff's department.'

686
00:32:30,383 --> 00:32:32,298
Cho'll lead the search
of the state forest.

687
00:32:32,385 --> 00:32:34,082
We'll start
at the Flint property line.

688
00:32:34,169 --> 00:32:36,563
One hour. Come on.

689
00:32:38,478 --> 00:32:40,219
[pants and sighs]

690
00:32:43,352 --> 00:32:45,267
See, that's how you do
a psychic reading?

691
00:32:45,354 --> 00:32:47,139
[clicks tongue]

692
00:32:47,226 --> 00:32:48,270
[blinds rattle]

693
00:32:48,357 --> 00:32:51,056
Whew.

694
00:32:51,143 --> 00:32:53,536
[yawns]

695
00:32:56,844 --> 00:32:59,499
[birds chirping]

696
00:33:25,220 --> 00:33:27,309
Drop the knife!
Do it now!

697
00:33:27,396 --> 00:33:29,964
Are you deaf?
Drop it, Flint!

698
00:33:30,051 --> 00:33:32,140
I wasn't gonna hurt him,
I swear.

699
00:33:32,227 --> 00:33:34,621
Get on your knees.
Put your hands on your head.

700
00:33:41,758 --> 00:33:42,716
[opens latch]

701
00:33:42,803 --> 00:33:43,760
[clicks]

702
00:33:52,030 --> 00:33:55,337
Conner, I'm agent Van Pelt.
I'm from the CBI.

703
00:33:55,424 --> 00:33:56,773
I'm here to help you.

704
00:33:56,860 --> 00:33:57,861
Are you okay?

705
00:33:57,948 --> 00:33:58,906
Yeah.

706
00:34:01,039 --> 00:34:02,257
Ohh.

707
00:34:02,344 --> 00:34:04,129
[Jonathan]
'I was just looking for Conner.'

708
00:34:04,216 --> 00:34:07,088
This is all
a big misunderstanding.

709
00:34:07,175 --> 00:34:09,003
You wanted Conner dead.

710
00:34:09,090 --> 00:34:12,702
You grabbed him, made it look
like a child murderer did it.

711
00:34:12,789 --> 00:34:14,443
Which part are
we misunderstanding?

712
00:34:14,530 --> 00:34:15,923
But you couldn't
bring yourself

713
00:34:16,010 --> 00:34:18,404
to kill your baby brother
face-to-face

714
00:34:18,491 --> 00:34:20,797
so you left him
in that duck blind.

715
00:34:20,884 --> 00:34:22,538
No food, no water,
no chance.

716
00:34:22,625 --> 00:34:24,323
No, that's not true.

717
00:34:24,410 --> 00:34:27,108
Why would I want Conner dead?
I don't need his money.

718
00:34:27,195 --> 00:34:29,110
Love.

719
00:34:29,197 --> 00:34:32,157
You are in love with Beth.

720
00:34:32,244 --> 00:34:36,683
- What are you thinking?
- Uh, I was thinking..

721
00:34:36,770 --> 00:34:38,119
Love is strange.

722
00:34:40,426 --> 00:34:42,558
Jane called this one right.

723
00:34:42,645 --> 00:34:45,866
He was in love with Beth, only
she didn't see him that way.

724
00:34:45,953 --> 00:34:48,173
- How was he gonna change that?
- Kill her kid.

725
00:34:48,260 --> 00:34:50,436
Be there to comfort her,
pick the broken pieces.

726
00:34:50,523 --> 00:34:52,786
- No! I always planned--
- 'Always planned what?'

727
00:34:52,873 --> 00:34:54,788
What did you plan?

728
00:34:54,875 --> 00:34:56,659
[sighs]

729
00:34:59,836 --> 00:35:02,187
[sighs]

730
00:35:02,274 --> 00:35:05,581
I had always planned to go get
him and bring him back.

731
00:35:05,668 --> 00:35:07,322
Play the hero.

732
00:35:09,455 --> 00:35:12,153
Put on a mask,
kidnap Conner

733
00:35:12,240 --> 00:35:14,634
then go find him later,
rescue him.

734
00:35:14,721 --> 00:35:17,158
And then Beth is filled
with gratitude

735
00:35:17,245 --> 00:35:20,030
and falls
into your manly arms.

736
00:35:20,118 --> 00:35:21,815
- Bingo.
- That's a dumb plan.

737
00:35:21,902 --> 00:35:24,600
I was going
to bring him back!

738
00:35:26,820 --> 00:35:29,605
So what was the knife for?

739
00:35:29,692 --> 00:35:31,651
I..

740
00:35:31,738 --> 00:35:33,131
I didn't..

741
00:35:37,396 --> 00:35:41,139
Planning is easy.
Reality's a bit harder.

742
00:35:41,226 --> 00:35:45,012
What if Conner recognized you?
What if Jane is psychic?

743
00:35:45,099 --> 00:35:49,016
Better just to make a clean
break and kill the kid, right?

744
00:35:49,103 --> 00:35:51,584
He is.

745
00:35:51,671 --> 00:35:55,109
Jane's psychic.
Isn't he?

746
00:35:55,196 --> 00:35:56,545
Nah.

747
00:35:56,632 --> 00:36:00,419
We followed you.
You led us to Conner.

748
00:36:00,506 --> 00:36:01,724
No.

749
00:36:01,811 --> 00:36:03,291
No, no, no.
That's impossible.

750
00:36:03,378 --> 00:36:05,554
The stuff Mr. Jane said,
that he saw Conner.

751
00:36:05,641 --> 00:36:08,296
The-the trees,
the smell of gunpowder

752
00:36:08,383 --> 00:36:11,647
near a-a body of water..
It was all accurate.

753
00:36:11,734 --> 00:36:14,128
How the hell did he do it?

754
00:36:22,832 --> 00:36:25,226
- Mom. Mommy!
- Hi.

755
00:36:25,313 --> 00:36:27,750
[crying]
Hi, baby.

756
00:36:27,837 --> 00:36:29,622
Oh, baby, you're home.

757
00:36:29,709 --> 00:36:31,058
You're home. You're safe.

758
00:36:31,145 --> 00:36:33,495
Yeah, welcome home, buddy.

759
00:36:33,582 --> 00:36:35,845
'Ohh. Mm.'

760
00:36:35,932 --> 00:36:38,935
Look at you. Oh, my God.

761
00:36:39,022 --> 00:36:40,763
Oh. I'm just happy, okay?

762
00:36:40,850 --> 00:36:43,549
You want some French toast?
I made you some French toast.

763
00:36:43,636 --> 00:36:46,682
- French toast is for breakfast.
- It's a special occasion.

764
00:36:46,769 --> 00:36:48,510
Come on.

765
00:36:48,597 --> 00:36:49,946
[sniffles]
Come on.

766
00:36:52,166 --> 00:36:53,559
Congratulations, Mr. Jane.

767
00:36:53,646 --> 00:36:56,518
Oh. Yes, yes.

768
00:36:56,605 --> 00:36:59,826
You son of a bitch.
You trying to steal my action?

769
00:36:59,913 --> 00:37:02,959
Mr. Glass,
nice to finally meet you.

770
00:37:03,046 --> 00:37:06,049
And you got no action. You're
a disgrace to the profession.

771
00:37:06,136 --> 00:37:08,574
That contact
you faked with Conner..

772
00:37:08,661 --> 00:37:10,880
Weak. Weak.

773
00:37:10,967 --> 00:37:12,969
Bite me.
That gag was seamless.

774
00:37:13,056 --> 00:37:15,494
You see how she fell for it?

775
00:37:15,581 --> 00:37:18,323
[high-pitched]
"Oh. Mo mo. Mo mo."

776
00:37:18,410 --> 00:37:19,585
[laughs]

777
00:37:20,412 --> 00:37:21,848
[chuckles]

778
00:37:21,935 --> 00:37:23,806
Thanks. That should do it.

779
00:37:23,893 --> 00:37:25,504
Excuse me?

780
00:37:25,591 --> 00:37:28,507
[clears throat]
And, uh, stop.

781
00:37:28,594 --> 00:37:29,986
[beeps]

782
00:37:30,073 --> 00:37:32,598
[Glass on tape]
"Oh. Mo mo. Mo mo."

783
00:37:32,685 --> 00:37:35,557
[laughs]

784
00:37:35,644 --> 00:37:36,558
Bye.

785
00:37:46,916 --> 00:37:48,222
Don't leave.

786
00:37:48,309 --> 00:37:50,529
I won't.
We'll be right over there.

787
00:37:50,616 --> 00:37:51,965
[sheets rustle]

788
00:37:55,490 --> 00:37:58,014
So..

789
00:37:58,101 --> 00:38:00,452
You gonna tell me
how you did it?

790
00:38:00,539 --> 00:38:03,193
Everything you said came true..

791
00:38:03,281 --> 00:38:06,588
...but it was a trick,
wasn't it?

792
00:38:06,675 --> 00:38:07,589
Yeah.

793
00:38:09,635 --> 00:38:10,592
How?

794
00:38:13,595 --> 00:38:15,467
Well, um..

795
00:38:17,251 --> 00:38:20,602
Being held not far from home..

796
00:38:20,689 --> 00:38:22,169
...the police shut down
the roads

797
00:38:22,256 --> 00:38:23,736
immediately
after Conner's abduction.

798
00:38:23,823 --> 00:38:25,781
The lake..

799
00:38:25,868 --> 00:38:28,784
There's always a body
of water nearby, always.

800
00:38:28,871 --> 00:38:31,265
Trees, leaves, earth..

801
00:38:31,352 --> 00:38:33,441
There was, uh,
white fir pollen

802
00:38:33,528 --> 00:38:36,792
found at, uh,
at the bus stop

803
00:38:36,879 --> 00:38:39,621
and where could you hide
anyone in a forest?

804
00:38:39,708 --> 00:38:43,103
Hunting blind,
hence the gunpowder smell.

805
00:38:43,190 --> 00:38:46,411
And I was watching
Jonathan's face the whole time.

806
00:38:46,498 --> 00:38:50,676
I could see whenever
my guesses landed.

807
00:38:51,807 --> 00:38:54,506
[sighs]
Of course.

808
00:38:56,029 --> 00:38:57,813
Elegant.

809
00:39:03,210 --> 00:39:05,908
You know,
all those years ago

810
00:39:05,995 --> 00:39:07,170
when you were a psychic

811
00:39:07,257 --> 00:39:10,913
and...you were lying to me

812
00:39:11,000 --> 00:39:12,524
telling me about my future--

813
00:39:12,611 --> 00:39:14,700
Yeah, I'm-I'm very sorry
about that.

814
00:39:14,787 --> 00:39:16,789
Don't apologize.

815
00:39:16,876 --> 00:39:20,053
You tried to tell me.

816
00:39:20,140 --> 00:39:22,838
You deceived me, sure..

817
00:39:22,925 --> 00:39:25,101
[sighs]

818
00:39:25,188 --> 00:39:27,190
...but you gave me hope.

819
00:39:31,847 --> 00:39:33,719
Thank you for that.

820
00:39:39,507 --> 00:39:40,856
Goodbye, Patrick.

821
00:39:42,118 --> 00:39:43,468
Bye, Beth.

822
00:40:04,837 --> 00:40:06,447
[sighs]

823
00:40:06,534 --> 00:40:09,276
- Cheer up.
- Oh, I'm cheery.

824
00:40:09,363 --> 00:40:11,321
You heard her.
You gave her hope.

825
00:40:11,409 --> 00:40:13,323
I didn't give her hope.

826
00:40:13,411 --> 00:40:15,848
I sold her hope.

827
00:40:15,935 --> 00:40:18,198
I think hope is worth it
at any price.

828
00:40:18,285 --> 00:40:19,982
What, are you running
for office now?

829
00:40:20,069 --> 00:40:21,593
Okay, you know what?

830
00:40:21,680 --> 00:40:24,117
You're a wicked charlatan,
and you're going to hell then.

831
00:40:24,204 --> 00:40:27,163
That's more like it. I'll save
you a seat by the fire.

832
00:40:27,250 --> 00:40:28,904
Oh, I'm not going to hell.

833
00:40:28,991 --> 00:40:30,384
- Oh, you're not?
- 'No.'

834
00:40:30,471 --> 00:40:31,994
You've made
other arrangements, huh?

835
00:40:32,081 --> 00:40:35,128
- 'Mm-hmm.'
- 'Yeah, where are you going?'

836
00:40:35,215 --> 00:40:37,130
[Lisbon]
'Do you really wanna have
this conversation?'

837
00:40:37,217 --> 00:40:40,263
'You ready for some,
uh, theological talk here?'

838
00:40:40,350 --> 00:40:42,309
[Jane]
'I don't reallywanna
have that conversation.'

839
00:40:42,396 --> 00:40:44,398
[Lisbon]
'You wanted to feel better,
not worse.'

840
00:40:44,485 --> 00:40:46,661
[Jane]
'I'm gonna recline
and have a little sleep.'

841
00:40:46,748 --> 00:40:48,097
[Lisbon]
'Okay.'

